sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Clinician / Records Officer
    participant Web as Next.js 15 (ECS Fargate)
    participant DB as RDS PostgreSQL 16 (RLS)
    participant S3 as Amazon S3 (SSE-KMS)
    participant SQS1 as SQS: document-ingest
    participant L1 as Lambda: document-ingest
    participant OCR as LocalPDF / Textract / Sarvam Vision
    participant SQS2 as SQS: ocr-result
    participant L2 as Lambda: ocr-result
    participant LLM as RuleExtractor + Bedrock Nova

    User->>Web: POST /api/v1/patients/[id]/documents/upload-url
    Web->>DB: withTenant(orgId): reserveDocumentForUpload (status='pending_upload')
    Web-->>User: Return 900s Presigned S3 PUT URL (max 25 MB)
    User->>S3: Direct PUT PDF bytes (SSE-KMS encrypted)
    S3->>SQS1: s3:ObjectCreated:* event (org/ prefix)
    SQS1->>L1: Trigger documentIngestHandler (batch_size=1)
    L1->>S3: Stream object & compute content_sha256
    L1->>DB: Check SHA-256 duplicate within (org_id, patient_id)
    alt Byte-Identical Duplicate Found
        L1->>DB: Mark duplicate_status='duplicate_candidate' & skip OCR
    else Unique Document
        L1->>OCR: Try LocalMultimodalOcrAdapter (born-digital PDF) or start Textract/Sarvam
        OCR->>SQS2: Completion notification / normalized pages
        SQS2->>L2: Trigger ocrResultHandler (batch_size=2)
        L2->>DB: Insert immutable document_page & locked text_span rows
        L2->>LLM: Extract structured facts (RuleBasedExtractor + Bedrock Converse tool)
        L2->>L2: Enforce Stage A (validateSpans) & Stage B (validateCandidateProvenance)
        L2->>DB: Insert evidence_fact ('extracted'), ledger_entry (SHA-256), detectConflicts(), computeReadiness()
    end
